.TITLE "top"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Provides a dynamic, real-time view of the running system. It displays __system summary__ information and a list of processes currently being managed by the Linux kernel.

.DIV "TLDR"
**top**
Starts the interactive process monitor with the default settings.
> 

**top -u user**
Displays only the processes owned by a specific user.
> __-u__ user flag | __user__ the target username

**top -p pid**
Monitors only a specific process identified by its PID.
> __-p__ pid flag | __pid__ the Process ID to monitor

.DIV "SUMMARY"
While __top__ is running, you can press __k__ to kill a process or __q__ to exit. It is an essential tool for diagnosing performance issues and identifying processes that are consuming too much CPU or memory.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:htop** **linux:ps** **linux:vmstat**

documentation: __https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/top.1.html__
